# What CLDR release 49 says of the languages it has data for, which
# `fallback_chain` and the subpackages read: the parent locales, the script
# each language is likely written in and the regions that choose another,
# each language's likely region, and the tags RFC 5646 calls grandfathered
# with the tags CLDR replaces them with.
#
# Generated, never edited by hand: the Heroes program `rebel/generators/i18n_core/`
# read CLDR 49's JSON, `cldr-49.0.0-json-full.zip` of
# https://github.com/unicode-org/cldr-json/releases/download/49.0.0/
# (SHA-256
# 3b1f5d684d29c541d3acf91fe834b3fe36ae0f34775e3ee50e93558bf14ca174,
# fetched 2026-11-21), its files `cldr-core/availableLocales.json` and
# `supplemental/likelySubtags.json`, `parentLocales.json` and
# `aliases.json`, and wrote this module whole; its `check` command says
# whether this module is still what it writes.

